sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant KServe as KServe Gateway
    participant API as vLLM API Server<br/>OpenAI-compatible
    participant Sched as Request Scheduler
    participant Engine as Model Execution Engine
    participant Plugin as vllm_gaudi Plugin<br/>HpuPlatform
    participant HPU as Intel Gaudi HPU<br/>via SynapseAI 1.23.0
    participant Ray as Ray Workers<br/>(multi-HPU)
    participant Storage as Model Storage<br/>(PVC / S3)

    Note over Client, Storage: Inference Request Flow

    Client->>KServe: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>or /v1/completions
    KServe->>API: Forward HTTP request<br/>(routing & scaling managed by KServe)
    API->>API: Validate request<br/>Optional API key check (--api-key)
    API->>Sched: Enqueue inference request
    Sched->>Engine: Schedule batch for execution

    Note over Engine, HPU: First request triggers model load

    opt Model Loading (first request)
        Engine->>Storage: Load model weights
        Storage-->>Engine: Model artifacts
        Engine->>Plugin: Initialize HpuPlatform
        Plugin->>HPU: Allocate HPU memory<br/>Load weights to device
    end

    Engine->>Plugin: Execute inference<br/>(attention, MoE, quantization)
    Plugin->>HPU: Dispatch HPU kernels<br/>(FP8/GPTQ/AWQ quantized ops)

    opt Distributed Inference (multi-HPU)
        Plugin->>Ray: Orchestrate workers
        Ray->>HPU: Parallel execution
        HPU-->>Ray: Partial results
        Ray->>Plugin: HCCL all-reduce
    end

    opt Disaggregated Prefill/Decode
        Plugin->>Plugin: NIXL KV cache transfer<br/>(prefill → decode stage)
    end

    HPU-->>Plugin: Inference result
    Plugin-->>Engine: Generated tokens
    Engine-->>Sched: Completed batch
    Sched-->>API: Streaming / complete response
    API-->>KServe: JSON response
    KServe-->>Client: HTTP response<br/>(OpenAI-format JSON)
